{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.MoebiusThreePointRigidity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.MoebiusThreePointRigidity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MoebiusThreePointRigidity.moebius_proportional_of_three_agree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MoebiusThreePointRigidity.moebius_proportional_of_three_agree","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MoebiusThreePointRigidity.lean#L121-L145","doc":"**The injectivity `Stab(B) ↪ Sym(B)`, in cleared coordinates.**\n\nIf two Möbius data agree at three distinct points — cleared, `(a·x + b)·(c'·x + d') =\n(a'·x + b')·(c·x + d)` — then every `2×2` minor of the stacked data vanishes:\n\n  `a·c' = a'·c`,  `a·d' + b·c' = a'·d + b'·c`,  `b·d' = b'·d`\n\ni.e. the two data are proportional and induce the same map. This is the statement the\n`Stab(B) ↪ Sym(B) = S₆` embedding rests on: a base automorphism preserving the six-point\nbranch locus is pinned by where it sends three of those points, so the stabiliser is\nfinite of order at most `6·5·4`.\n\nSame lemma again — the difference of the two cleared forms is a quadratic in the\nevaluation point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MoebiusThreePointRigidity.moebius_id_of_three_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MoebiusThreePointRigidity.moebius_id_of_three_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MoebiusThreePointRigidity.lean#L104-L119","doc":"**Three-point rigidity.** If the Möbius data `(a, b; c, d)` fixes three distinct\npoints — in the cleared sense `a·w + b = w·(c·w + d)`, which needs no chart and no\n`cw + d ≠ 0` — then `c = 0`, `d = a` and `b = 0`: the data of the identity map.\n\nThis is the content #7185 deferred as \"Möbius machinery\"; the fixed-point condition is a\nquadratic `c·w² + (d−a)·w − b = 0`, so `quadratic_zero_of_three_roots` does all of it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MoebiusThreePointRigidity.quadratic_zero_of_three_roots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MoebiusThreePointRigidity.quadratic_zero_of_three_roots","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MoebiusThreePointRigidity.lean#L71-L102","doc":"**A quadratic with three distinct roots is the zero quadratic.**\n\n`A·x² + B·x + C` vanishing at three pairwise-distinct points forces `A = B = C = 0`.\n\nProof: subtracting the equations at `x` and `y` and cancelling `x − y` gives\n`A·(x+y) + B = 0`; the same at `x` and `z` gives `A·(x+z) + B = 0`; subtracting those and\ncancelling `y − z` gives `A = 0`, and the rest follows. ","signatureChunk":0}]}